practiceProblems.problemStatement:
A service crashes with `ConcurrentModificationException`:
```java
List<String> logs = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList("INFO", "DEBUG", "ERROR", "DEBUG"));
for (String log : logs) {
    if (log.equals("DEBUG")) {
        logs.remove(log); // CRASH!
    }
}
```

Your Task:
1. Refactor the method to safely purge `"DEBUG"` entries using either `Iterator.remove()` or `logs.removeIf(...)`.
2. In `Main.main()`, print the purged logs:
   `Production Logs: [INFO, ERROR]`

practiceProblems.solutionCode:
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> logs = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList("INFO", "DEBUG", "ERROR", "DEBUG"));
        logs.removeIf(log -> log.equals("DEBUG"));
        System.out.println("Production Logs: " + logs);
    }
}

